se, formerly the Flag House & Star-Spangled Banner Museum, is a museum located in the Jonestown/Old Town and adjacent to Little Italy neighborhoods of eastern downtown Baltimore, Maryland, United States.","wpu":"Flag House & Star-Spangled Banner Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Flag_House%2C_844_East_Pratt_Street%2C_Baltimore%2C_Maryland.JPG/960px-Flag_House%2C_844_East_Pratt_Street%2C_Baltimore%2C_Maryland.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"USCGC Taney","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":39.28578,"lo":-76.606294,"d":3234,"w":"https://historicships.org/explore/uscgc-cutter37","ds":"Roger B. Taney’s name removed from historic Pearl Harbor ship in Baltimore. Baltimore Sun. 2 July 2020.","ad":"Pier 5","f":["free"]},{"n":"Reginald F Lewis Museum of Maryland African-American History and Culture","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":39.287477,"lo":-76.603885,"d":3236,"h":"Mo 10:00-17:00; Th-We 10:00-17:00; Sa 10:00-17:00; Su 12:00-17:00","w":"https://www.lewismuseum.org/","wp":"en:Reginald F. Lewis Museum of Maryland African American History & Culture","wd":"Q7308685","ad":"830 East Pratt Street","ds":"The Reginald F. Lewis Museum of Maryland African American History & Culture is a resource in Baltimore, Maryland, for information about the lives and history of African American Marylanders. Its collections comprise 400 years of Maryland history and include more than 11,000 objects, artifacts, documents and photographs. The museum opened in 2005 and is an affiliate of the Smithsonian Institution.","wpu":"Reginald F. Lewis Museum of Maryland African American History & Culture","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Reginald_F._Lewis_Museum_of_Maryland_African_American_History_%26_Culture.jpg/960px-Reginald_F._Lewis_Museum_of_Maryland_African_American_History_%26_Culture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"MAXgallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":39.293832,"lo":-76.585885,"d":3245,"h":"Fr 16:00-19:00; Sa 16:00-19:00 || \"by appointment\"","w":"https://www.maxgallery.us/","ph":"+1 410-804-7459","ad":"126 North Madeira Street"},{"n":"National Aquarium","g":"sights","k":"aquarium","la":39.28517,"lo":-76.607769,"d":3277,"w":"https://aqua.org/","ph":"+1 410-576-3800","wp":"en:National Aquarium (Baltimore)","wd":"Q1000257","ad":"501 East Pratt Street","f":["wc"],"ds":"The National Aquarium—also known as the National Aquarium in Baltimore or Baltimore Aquarium—is a nonprofit public aquarium located at 501 East Pratt Street on Pier 3 in the Inner Harbor area of Downtown Baltimore, Maryland, United States. Constructed during a period of urban renewal in Baltimore, the aquarium opened on August 8, 1981.","wpu":"National Aquarium (Baltimore)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/National_Aquarium_Night_Aerial_2022.jpg/960px-National_Aquarium_Night_Aerial_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Maryland Science Center","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":39.281521,"lo":-76.611995,"d":3310,"h":"Mo-Tu closed; We-Fr 10:00-16:00; Sa-Su 10:00-17:00; Jul 4 10:00-17:00; Dec 25 closed","w":"https://www.mdsci.org/","ph":"+1 410-685-2370","wp":"en:Maryland Science Center","wd":"Q3296288","ds":"The Maryland Science Center (MSC), located in Baltimore's Inner Harbor, opened to the public in 1976. It includes three levels of exhibits, a planetarium, and an observatory. It was one of the original structures that drove the revitalization of the Baltimore Inner Harbor from its industrial roots to a thriving downtown destination.","ad":"601 Light Street","f":["wc"],"wpu":"Maryland Science Center","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/23/Maryland_Science_Center_logo_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"USS Torsk","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":39.284954,"lo":-76.608713,"d":3321,"w":"https://historicships.org/","wp":"en:USS Torsk","wd":"Q7874823","ds":"USS Torsk (hull number SS-423), is a Tench-class submarine built for the United States Navy during World War II, currently part of the museum ship fleet of Historic Ships in Baltimore. Armed with ten torpedo tubes, the Tench-class submarines were incremental developments of the highly-successful Gato-class submarines that formed the backbone of the US Navy's submarine force during the war.","wpu":"USS Torsk","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/USS_TORSK_%28submarine%29_taken_from_walking_bridge.JPG/960px-USS_TORSK_%28submarine%29_taken_from_walking_bridge.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jewish Museum of Maryland","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":39.29024,"lo":-76.601137,"d":3344,"w":"https://jewishmuseummd.org/","ph":"+1 410 732 6400","wp":"en:Jewish Museum of Maryland","wd":"Q6189893","ad":"15 Lloyd Street","f":["wc"],"ds":"The Jewish Museum of Maryland is located in the Jonestown neighborhood of Baltimore, Maryland, United States. The museum tells the story of the American Jewish experience in the city of Baltimore and throughout the US state of Maryland.","wpu":"Jewish Museum of Maryland","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Jewish_Museum_of_Maryland%2C_Lloyd_St.%2C_Baltimore_City%2C_Maryland.JPG/960px-Jewish_Museum_of_Maryland%2C_Lloyd_St.%2C_Baltimore_City%2C_Maryland.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Church Hospital","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":39.293028,"lo":-76.594167,"d":3346,"wp":"en:Church Home and Hospital","wd":"Q5116628","ds":"Church Home and Hospital (formerly the Church Home and Infirmary) was a hospital in Baltimore, located on Broadway, between East Fayette and East Baltimore Streets, on Washington Hill, several blocks south of the Johns Hopkins Hospital, that also operated a long-term care facility. It was affiliated with the Episcopal Diocese of Maryland of the Episcopal Church (United States).","wpu":"Church Home and Hospital"},{"n":"1840s Carrollton Inn","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":39.288745,"lo":-76.604107,"d":3358,"w":"https://www.1840splaza.com/","ph":"+14103851840","wd":"Q4554563","ad":"50 Albemarle Street","wifi":1},{"n":"Thomas Wildey Monument","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":39.293285,"lo":-76.593959,"d":3366},{"n":"Chesapeake","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":39.285683,"lo":-76.60878,"d":3380,"w":"https://historicships.org/","wp":"en:United States lightship Chesapeake (LV-116)","wd":"Q7892539","ds":"United States lightship Chesapeake (LS-116/WAL-538/WLV-538) is a museum ship owned by the National Park Service and on a 25-year loan to Baltimore City, and is operated by Historic Ships in Baltimore Museum in Baltimore, Maryland. A National Historic Landmark, she is one of a small number of preserved lightships.","wpu":"United States lightship Chesapeake (LV-116)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Lightship_Chesapeake_Baltimore_MD1.jpg/960px-Lightship_Chesapeake_Baltimore_MD1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"SK Cleaners","g":"essentials","k":"dry_cleaning","la":39.279934,"lo":-76.575695,"d":1701},{"n":"PNC Bank","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":39.26937,"lo":-76.599237,"d":1725},{"n":"Verizon","g":"essentials","k":"mobile_phone","la":39.269264,"lo":-76.599321,"d":1729},{"n":"Bank of America","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":39.280185,"lo":-76.575555,"d":1731,"h":"24/7"},{"n":"Harris Teeter Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":39.275029,"lo":-76.564512,"d":1738},{"n":"M&T Bank","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":39.268279,"lo":-76.599898,"d":1751,"w":"https://locations.mtb.com/md/baltimore/bank-branches-and-atms-baltimore-md-3104.html","ad":"1725 Whetstone Way"},{"n":"T-Mobile","g":"essentials","k":"mobile_phone","la":39.280773,"lo":-76.57999,"d":1753,"w":"https://www.t-mobile.com/stores/bd/t-mobile-baltimo