g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.2622,"lo":-76.5715,"d":795,"ds":"The Lazaretto Point Light was a historic lighthouse in Baltimore harbor. Though long demolished, a replica stands near its original site.","wpu":"Lazaretto Point Light","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e9/Lazaretto_point_light.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"St. Michael the Archangel Ukrainian Catholic Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.285739,"lo":-76.582583,"d":2316,"ds":"St. Michael the Archangel Ukrainian Catholic Church is a Ukrainian Catholic church located in Baltimore, Maryland. It was founded to initially serve the needs of the Ukrainian immigrant community in Baltimore.","wpu":"St. Michael the Archangel Ukrainian Catholic Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/St._Michael_the_Archangel_Ukrainian_Catholic_Church_01.JPG/960px-St._Michael_the_Archangel_Ukrainian_Catholic_Church_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Holy Rosary Church (Baltimore)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.286567,"lo":-76.587269,"d":2478,"ds":"Holy Rosary Church is a Roman Catholic church located within the Archdiocese of Baltimore in Fells Point, Baltimore, Maryland. It was established to serve Baltimore's Polish community. Cardinal Karol Wojtyła (later Pope John Paul II) prayed at the shrine during a visit in 1976.","wpu":"Holy Rosary Church (Baltimore)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Holy_Rosary_Church_Baltimore.JPG/960px-Holy_Rosary_Church_Baltimore.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Riverside Park (Baltimore)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.270278,"lo":-76.608056,"d":2485,"ds":"Riverside Park is a nearly 17-acre (6.9 ha) public park located in the historic Riverside neighborhood in Baltimore, Maryland. The park is also known as Leone Riverside Park.","wpu":"Riverside Park (Baltimore)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Entrance_to_Riverside_Park%2C_Baltimore_MD%2C_Sep_2013.jpg/960px-Entrance_to_Riverside_Park%2C_Baltimore_MD%2C_Sep_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Patterson Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.2878,"lo":-76.5786,"d":2538,"ds":"Patterson Park is an urban park in Southeast Baltimore, Maryland, United States, adjacent to the neighborhoods of Canton, Highlandtown, Patterson Park, and Butchers Hill. It is bordered by East Baltimore Street, Eastern Avenue, South Patterson Park Avenue, and South Linwood Avenue.","wpu":"Patterson Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Patterson_Park_October_Aerial.jpg/960px-Patterson_Park_October_Aerial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Mary, Star of the Sea (Baltimore)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.273889,"lo":-76.608889,"d":2676,"ds":"St. Mary, Star of the Sea is a Roman Catholic Church in the Federal Hill South neighborhood of Baltimore, Maryland. The church venerates Stella Maris, Our Lady, Star of the Sea, and carries a beacon atop its spire to welcome sailors to the Port of Baltimore.","wpu":"St. Mary, Star of the Sea (Baltimore)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/St._Mary%2C_Star_of_the_Sea_%28Church%2C_Baltimore%2C_MD%29.jpg/960px-St._Mary%2C_Star_of_the_Sea_%28Church%2C_Baltimore%2C_MD%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Legg Mason Tower","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.282583,"lo":-76.601611,"d":2698,"ds":"Legg Mason Tower is a 24-story glass high-rise located at 100 International Drive in Baltimore's Harbor East development. The building is currently known as the 100 International Drive building since the sale of Legg Mason to Franklin Templeton in 2020.","wpu":"Legg Mason Tower","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/68/Legg_mason_tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Holy Cross Roman Catholic Church (Baltimore)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":39.276111,"lo":-76.611111,"d":2949,"ds":"Holy Cross Roman Catholic Church is a historic Roman Catholic church complex located within the Archdiocese of Baltimore in the Federal Hill neighborhood of Baltimore, Maryland, United States.","wpu":"Holy Cross Roman Catholic Church (Baltimore)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Holy_Cross_Roman_Catholic_Church_Baltimore_MD_Dec_11.JPG/960px-Holy_Cross_Roman_Catholic_Church_Baltimore_MD_Dec_11.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Baltimore, also known as Baltimore City and Charm City is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Maryland. It is the 30th-most-populous U.S. city, with a population of 585,708 at the 2020 census and estimated at 569,997 in 2025; the Baltimore metropolitan area, at 2.86 million residents, is the 22nd-largest metropolitan area in the nation. The city is also part of the Washington–Baltimore combined statistical area, which had a population of 9.97 million in 2020.","wpu":"Baltimore","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Fell%27s_Point_Aerial_2022.jpg/960px-Fell%27s_Point_Aerial_2022.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-26"}